---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { GET_STARTED } from '../config';
import '../styles/home.css';

// The proof is copied from the recorded example "chat-default" (recorded 2 Oct 2026).
const proof = {
  prompt: 'Explain in two sentences why the sky is blue.',
  reply: "Sunlight entering Earth's atmosphere scatters off air molecules, and shorter blue wavelengths scatter much more strongly than longer red ones (a process called Rayleigh scattering). This scattered blue light is then distributed across the sky in all directions, so no matter where you look, you see blue.",
};
---
<Base title="Azizam: your own AI gateway" description="Your own AI gateway, shared on your terms. Put the AI engines you run, and any paid providers you choose, behind one OpenAI-compatible address." bodyClass="home">
  <main id="content" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="home-title">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <p class="eyebrow">Self-hosted AI gateway</p>
        <h1 id="home-title"><span class="accent-words">Your own</span> AI gateway, shared on your terms.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Put the AI engines you run, and any paid providers you choose, behind one OpenAI-compatible address. Give each person and app its own key, access plan and spend cap.</p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" data-cta href={GET_STARTED}>Get started</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" data-cta href="/examples/">See it work →</a>
        </div>
        <p class="microline">Runs on a computer you control · Works with OpenAI, Anthropic and Ollama clients · Private preview</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="proof-card card" aria-labelledby="proof-caption">
        <figcaption id="proof-caption" class="eyebrow">A real request, recorded through Azizam</figcaption>
        <p class="proof-request"><code class="proof-path"><span>POST</span> /openai/v1/chat/completions</code><code class="proof-model">default</code></p>
        <dl class="proof-exchange">
          <dt>You</dt>
          <dd>{proof.prompt}</dd>
          <dt>Reply</dt>
          <dd>{proof.reply}</dd>
        </dl>
        <p class="proof-meta">Ran in 4.3 s · 115 tokens · recorded 2 Oct 2026 · <a href="/examples/">More examples</a></p>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="block wrap" aria-labelledby="values-title">
      <h2 id="values-title" class="visually-hidden">What the gateway gives you</h2>
      <div class="value-grid">
        <article class="value-card card">
          <h3>A key and a plan for everyone</h3>
          <p>Invite people with a link. Each person and app gets its own key, and a plan that sets which models it may use and how much it may spend.</p>
          <div class="mini mini-plan" role="group" aria-label="Example plan: Family, Chat and Image, $5 a month"><span class="pill plan-name">Family</span><span class="pill">Chat</span><span class="pill">Image</span><span class="price">$5 a month</span></div>
        </article>
        <article class="value-card card">
          <h3>Your engines first</h3>
          <p>Requests go to the engines on your own hardware. A paid model is used only when the plan allows it, under a spend cap you set.</p>
          <div class="mini mini-path" role="group" aria-label="Your engine, then a paid provider only if allowed"><span>Your engine</span><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>Paid provider <small>(only if allowed)</small></span></div>
        </article>
        <article class="value-card card">
          <h3>A receipt for every request</h3>
          <p>See who asked, which model ran, where it ran and what it cost.</p>
          <div class="mini mini-receipt" role="group" aria-label="Receipt fields: Person, Model, Where it ran, Cost"><span>Person</span><span>Model</span><span>Where it ran</span><span>Cost</span></div>
        </article>
        <article class="value-card card">
          <h3>Works with the apps you already use</h3>
          <p>OpenAI, Anthropic and Ollama API shapes, and an MCP server for agents, on one address.</p>
          <p class="mini mini-routes" role="group" aria-label="Supported routes: OpenAI, Anthropic, Ollama and MCP"><code>/openai/v1</code> <code>/anthropic</code> <code>/ollama</code> <code>/mcp</code></p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="block wrap" aria-labelledby="how-title">
      <h2 id="how-title">How it works</h2>
      <figure class="flow" aria-labelledby="flow-caption">
        <figcaption id="flow-caption">Azizam checks the key and plan, sends the request to an engine or provider the plan allows, and records a receipt.</figcaption>
        <div class="flow-step">
          <p class="flow-title">Your apps and people</p>
          <p class="flow-detail">Chat apps, SDKs, coding agents, MCP clients, a phone</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-link"><span>one address, one key each</span></div>
        <div class="flow-step flow-gateway">
          <p class="flow-title">Azizam</p>
          <p class="flow-detail">Checks the key and access plan, routes the request, records a receipt</p>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-link"><span>only what the plan allows</span></div>
        <div class="flow-ends">
          <div class="flow-step">
            <p class="flow-title">Engines you run</p>
            <p class="flow-detail">Chat, image, video, speech and music servers on your hardware</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flow-step">
            <p class="flow-title">Providers you choose</p>
            <p class="flow-detail">Paid models, with spend caps</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="block wrap" aria-labelledby="start-title">
      <h2 id="start-title">Start in a few minutes</h2>
      <div class="early card" id="early-access">
        <p class="eyebrow">Early access</p>
        <p class="lead">Azizam is in private preview.</p>
        <p>Access is by invitation for now.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="after-access">Once you have access:</p>
      <div class="command-block card">
        <div class="command-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Installation method">
          <button id="compose-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="compose-panel" type="button">Docker Compose</button>
        </div>
        <div id="compose-panel" class="command-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="compose-tab">
          <pre tabindex="0"><code id="compose-command">docker compose up -d</code></pre>
          <button class="copy-btn" id="copy-command" type="button" hidden>Copy</button>
        </div>
        <p id="copy-status" class="visually-hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>
      <ol class="quick-steps">
        <li>Open http://127.0.0.1:5000/setup and create the owner account.</li>
        <li>Add your engine's address and give its model a name.</li>
        <li>Create a key, point your app at <code>/openai/v1</code>, and send a message.</li>
      </ol>
      <p><a href={GET_STARTED}>Read the setup guide</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="block wrap" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
      <h2 id="limits-title">Before you rely on it</h2>
      <ul class="facts">
        <li>You choose the engines and model files. Azizam connects to them; it does not download models.</li>
        <li>Compatibility is per route. Each <a href="/docs/api/">API page</a> lists the features that work and their limits.</li>
        <li>Paid spend is estimated, reserved, then settled; final cost may remain unknown. Running requests can pass a cap; set a provider credit limit too.</li>
        <li>You run the computer, including updates, backups and HTTPS for access from other devices.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>
  <script>
    const button = document.getElementById('copy-command');
    const status = document.getElementById('copy-status');
    const command = document.getElementById('compose-command');
    if (button && status && command) {
      button.hidden = false;
      button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(command.textContent ?? '');
          status.textContent = 'Command copied';
          button.textContent = 'Copied';
        } catch {
          status.textContent = 'Copy failed. Select the command and copy it.';
          button.textContent = 'Select and copy';
        }
      });
    }
  </script>
</Base>
